WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.810
Hold a magnifying
glass close to a page,

2
00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.630
and the print looks bigger
and the right way up.

3
00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:08.910
Now hold the same lens between
a sheet of white paper and a

4
00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:10.970
bright window across the room.

5
00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:13.890
On the paper appears a tiny
picture of the window.

6
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:15.770
It's upside down.

7
00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:18.490
Same lens, very different pictures.

8
00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:21.050
So how can one lens do both?

9
00:00:21.100 --> 00:00:24.650
In this mission, you'll see how
a converging lens brings light

10
00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:25.710
to a focus.

11
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:28.810
You'll find out what makes
an image real or virtual,

12
00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:31.710
and where the image forms.

13
00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:36.430
Your mission: find out how one
lens makes two kinds of image.
